  },
  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S1 imposes strict 24-hour reporting for all incidents and customer notice, exceeding safe requirements. S2 sets a 55°C test and 5% threshold but allows continued sales under corrective action, with only pass/fail disclosure to customers. S3 requires new units to have shut-off and a retrofit plan with completion no sooner than six years. S4 requires built-in suppression after 36 months with equivalent alternatives. S5 sets an 8/100k trigger for regulator review but leaves recall to regulator discretion, with prompt notice."
 },
